MATRIX: Integer to binary and hexadecimal. Digits are built from the remainder, most significant first via recursion.

ESCAPE THE MATRIX

HUSTLE digit WITH n
  IF n IS LESS THAN 10 THEN
    CASH OUT "" PLUS n
  PERIOD
  IF n IS THE SAME AS 10 THEN
    CASH OUT "A"
  PERIOD
  IF n IS THE SAME AS 11 THEN
    CASH OUT "B"
  PERIOD
  IF n IS THE SAME AS 12 THEN
    CASH OUT "C"
  PERIOD
  IF n IS THE SAME AS 13 THEN
    CASH OUT "D"
  PERIOD
  IF n IS THE SAME AS 14 THEN
    CASH OUT "E"
  PERIOD
  CASH OUT "F"
DONE HUSTLING

HUSTLE rebase WITH n AND base
  IF n IS LESS THAN base THEN
    CASH OUT CALL digit WITH n
  PERIOD
  CASH OUT (CALL rebase WITH (CALL floor WITH n DIVIDED BY base) AND base) PLUS CALL digit WITH n MODULO base
DONE HUSTLING

WHAT COLOR IS YOUR BUGATTI "42 in binary is " PLUS CALL rebase WITH 42 AND 2
WHAT COLOR IS YOUR BUGATTI "255 in hex is " PLUS CALL rebase WITH 255 AND 16
WHAT COLOR IS YOUR BUGATTI "2026 in hex is " PLUS CALL rebase WITH 2026 AND 16
WHAT COLOR IS YOUR BUGATTI "13 in base 3 is " PLUS CALL rebase WITH 13 AND 3

BUGATTI n EQUALS 1
BUGATTI powers EQUALS ""
GRIND WHILE n IS LESS THAN 17
  BUGATTI powers EQUALS powers PLUS (CALL rebase WITH n AND 2) PLUS " "
  BUGATTI n EQUALS n PLUS 1
STOP GRINDING
WHAT COLOR IS YOUR BUGATTI powers

